:HELP NAME='IFCSTS/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.5=Display details
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display details it.
:PT.8=Display associated routes
:PD.Type 8 next to an entry and press Enter to display associated routes
it.
:PT.9=Start
:PD.Type 9 next to an entry and press Enter to start it. The Start
TCP/IP Interface (STRTCPIFC) command runs for the entry.
:PT.10=End
:PD.Type 10 next to an entry and press Enter to end it. The End TCP/IP
Interface (ENDTCPIFC) command runs for the entry.
:PT.12=Work with configuration status
:PD.Type 12 next to an entry and press Enter to work with configuration
status it.
:PT.14=Display multicast groups
:PD.Type 14 next to an entry and press Enter to display multicast groups
it.
:EPARML.
