:HELP NAME='KEYS/JOBKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F6=Print
:PD.Prints the display.
:PT.F9=Command line
:PD.Shows a command line to run a command from.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F13=Information Assistant
:PD.Information Assistant.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JCTYPE'.Connection type
:P.The connection type shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JLADR'.Local address
:P.The local address shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JLPORT'.Local port
:P.The local port shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JRADR'.Remote address
:P.The remote address shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JRPORT'.Remote port
:P.The remote port shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJOBS/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JPAD'.JPAD
:P.The JPAD of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JNAME'.Name
:P.The name of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JUSER'.User
:P.The user of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JNBR'.Number
:P.The number of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JTYPE'.Type
:P.The type of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JCUR'.Current User
:P.The current User of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPJOBS/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.5=Work with job
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to work with job it. The
Work with Job (WRKJOB) command runs for the entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/STSKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F5=Refresh
